# the G12 negative-compilation proof's scratch copy of the tree (deleted on
# success). It sits at the port root rather than under test/ because the copy now
# carries test/ itself, and `fs.cpSync` refuses to copy a directory into a
# subdirectory of itself.
examples/typescript/.work/

# the TypeScript workspace wall's declaration output (npm run typecheck:wall).
# The wall's RED path also emits beside the source; scripts/wall.mjs sweeps that,
# deliberately rather than ignoring it — a tree in that state fails the NEXT run,
# so hiding it from git would hide a state the tree must never be in.
examples/typescript/.tsbuild/

